#
# Look-alikes for tools/release/redaction-scan.py (read by default).
# action | class | path glob | regex | reason
# action: drop (a look-alike, not counted) or info (listed, not a finding).
# class `*` is any class; the glob is fnmatch over the whole path ("*"
# matches across "/"); the regex is searched in the line and drops or lists
# the hits its match overlaps.  Patterns and public names only: a private
# value (login, lab, runner or bridge host, address) never goes here.
#
# Placeholders (docs/release/redaction-audit.md part 3).
drop | home-path | * | /(home|Users)/\.\.\. | elided path, not a user name
drop | login-at-host | * | root@BOARD\b | placeholder for the board's ssh target
drop | login-at-host | * | root@localhost\b | loopback through a tunnel
drop | login-at-host | tools/mali/panthor/tests/board_lock.rs | root[@]board-lock-test\b | test fixture for the lock's BOARD_HOST
drop | * | * | <(user|login)@(host|board)> | placeholder
# The RFC 1918 fixtures that the console redaction self-test rewrites.
drop | private-ipv4 | tools/board_selftest.sh | \b(10\.11\.12\.(1|13)|172\.16\.0\.9)\b | redact_dir fixture input (RFC 1918)
drop | private-ipv4 | tools/cts/pr-session-selftest.sh | secret-user@10\.9\.8\.7\b | fixture of the self-test's BOARD_HOST refusal
# Fixtures of the redaction self-tests and dry-run matrices that landed
# 2026-11-07 to 2026-11-09 (board.sh's pi5 rows, the NanoPC-T6 slice tools).
# A redaction test has to hold the input it redacts (an RFC 1918 or tailnet
# address, root@<placeholder>, an invented *.ts.net name), and a dry run has
# to name a fake board. Each rule is the fixture's own literal or an RFC 2606
# placeholder shape, so the same class anywhere else stays a finding.
drop | private-ipv4 | tools/board_selftest.sh | \b(100\.64\.7\.9|10\.20\.30\.40)\b | pi5 fixtures: the stub ssh's refused address and the console redaction input
drop | email | * | @[A-Za-z0-9.-]+\.example(?![A-Za-z0-9.-]) | .example placeholder host (RFC 2606), e.g. the dry runs' fake BOARD_HOST
drop | email | * | \bt@example\.com\b | a self-test's git identity (RFC 2606)
drop | home-path | tools/cts/mali-glmark2-selftest.sh | /board/home[/]yakogl-mali-glmark2\b | the fake board's home under the self-test's temp dir: the stage root, not a user
drop | private-ipv4 | tools/cts/mali-fail-triage.py | \b10\.1\.2\.3:22\b | scrub() self-test input
drop | login-at-host | tools/cts/mali-fail-triage.py | ssh root[@]nano at 10\.1\.2\.3:22 | scrub() self-test input: the whole invented string the test redacts
drop | private-ipv4 | tools/cts/mali-slice-readme-selftest.sh | ip="10\.1\.2\.3" | the dirty slice's address the README self-test expects reported
drop | login-at-host | * | root@board\b | placeholder for the board's prompt or ssh target (lower case)
drop | private-ipv4 | tools/cts/mali-slice-redact.py | \b100\.64\.0\.0/10\b | the tailnet range as a CIDR, in the class table
drop | private-ipv4 | tools/cts/mali-slice-redact.py | \b100\.64\.0\.9\b | self-test fixture of the tailnet class
drop | ipv6-local | tools/cts/mali-slice-redact.py | fe80:[:]1\b | the ipv6 class's example and fixture: the link-local prefix with no host part
drop | tailnet-dns | * | \bboard-1\.example\.ts\.net\b | an invented tailnet name with the RFC 2606 label, in the fixtures
drop | login-at-host | tools/cts/mali-slice-redact.py | root[@]192\.0\.2\.7\b | fixture: root at a documentation address (RFC 5737)
drop | email | tools/cts/mali-slice-redact.py | serial-getty@ttyS2\.service\b | a systemd unit instance named in the class table
drop | private-ipv4 | tools/cts/testdata/mali-fail-triage/* | \b10\.9\.8\.7\b | slice fixture: the address the triage redacts
drop | email | docs/notes/*.md | \b[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*@[0-9]+\.[xyzw]{1,4}\b | an IR operand reference (name, @, index, swizzle) in a quoted compiler dump
# The preflight selftest's fake BOARD_UART canary (a look-alike, never a real value).
drop | password | tools/cts/imx8mp-gles3-preflight-selftest.sh | SECRET\=ttyUSB | selftest fixture: the fake UART string the test asserts the preflight never prints
# Product defaults and keywords.
drop | som-serial | * | verdin-(am62p|imx8mp)-00000000 | zeroed serial: the product's default host name
drop | password | * | NOPASSWD: | sudoers keyword, not a password
drop | lab-host | * | \barmadillo\.local\b | the vendor's mDNS default host name
drop | lab-host | * | \byakogl-gate\b | the gate's public runner label
drop | lab-host | * | \bccfarm\b | the name of the farm tool
# tools/env/* drives the pool and image tool through its public interface:
# its CLI (`<tool> image build`, `<tool> pool apply`, `<tool> login`, `command
# -v <tool>`), its environment variables (`<TOOL>_RECIPES`, `<TOOL>_URL`), a
# session, CLI or pool of it, and its server's docs (`<tool>-complex`).
drop | lab-host | tools/env/* | \b[A-Za-z]+ (image|pool|login|session|CLI)\b|\bcommand -v [A-Za-z]+\b|\b[A-Z]+_(RECIPES|URL)\b|\b[A-Za-z]+-complex\b | the pool and image tool's CLI, environment variables, pools and server docs
# A compiled pattern bound to a name that contains "secret", not a value.
drop | password | *.py | \bSECRET\s*=\s*re\.compile\( | a regex named SECRET (the leak pattern a checker searches for)
# The scanner's self-description: lab-layout mentions in its own class table and pattern.
drop | lab-layout | tools/release/redaction-scan.py | \$HOME/com/github/|yakogl\-in\-rust | the class's own name, in the file that defines the class
# E-mail shapes that are no address of a person.
drop | * | * | @[A-Za-z0-9.-]+\.invalid\b | .invalid placeholder (RFC 2606)
drop | email | * | \bt@example\.org\b | a self-test's address
drop | email | * | \bgit@github\.com\b | the project's clone URL
drop | email | tools/testdata/* | @fa10000\.bootdev\.part_ | U-Boot device node in a console capture
drop | email | tools/testdata/* | @1000\.service\b | systemd unit name in a console capture
drop | email | docs/notes/pre-study-iq9075.md | @oss\.qualcomm\.com\b | Message-ID of an upstream patch series
# Upstream authors (information, not a finding).
info | email | * | \binfo@slint\.dev\b | upstream: the Slint licence contact
info | email | * | @kdab\.com\b | upstream: authors of the Slint sources the patch touches
info | email | driver/src/vivante/hw/*.xml.h | @ | upstream: authors of the etnaviv rules-ng headers
info | email | driver/src/v3d/* | \brobclark@freedesktop\.org\b | upstream: Mesa author of the code this file follows
info | email | tools/vivante/*.patch | @gmail\.com\b | upstream: etnaviv author in a Mesa patch
